      "writtenOn": "2023-10-30T08:30:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because apps have paired through createBond, it will send the data assuming that it is encrypted.\nIn general, apps do not always check whether the link is bonded or not when sending data.\n\nIf the encryption is released by key missing and the data is not transmitted due to it, the app is not known why it cannot communicate data without a callback related to success of encryption.\nTherefore, I think that BT stack have to send a callback related to enctyption success for the implementation you talked about.\nDo you think this structure is better?",
